<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Machchhu River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Machchhu is a river of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra peninsula</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, flowing north past Wankaner and Morbi towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-rann-of-kutch">Little Rann of Kutch</a>. The former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Wankaner and Morvi grew up on its banks. In August 1979 the failure of the Machchhu-II dam above Morbi during heavy rains sent a flood through the town that killed thousands of people, one of India's worst dam disasters.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/machchhu-river.jpg" alt="Machchhu River" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Camaal Mustafa Sikan… · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Another_view_from_the_Bridge_Morbi_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
